BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-179449@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260412T123152Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T183000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Impersonation" with Heidi Pitlor
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179449\n\nBookmark the date fo
 r a compelling conversation exploring Impersonation with Heidi Pitlor - a 
 sharp\, satirical novel about ambition\, motherhood\, and the blurred boun
 daries between identity and performance.\n\nAllie Lang is a professional g
 hostwriter and a perpetually broke single mother. After years of navigatin
 g the cultural expectations placed on mothers\, and the financial precarit
 y of her work\, she has grown wary of the stories she is asked to tell\, a
 nd the lives she is asked to inhabit.\n\nLana Breban is a formidable lawye
 r\, economist\, and rising political figure preparing for a run for office
 . When her team commissions a memoir to soften her public image\, Allie is
  hired to ghostwrite the story of Lana’s life as a mother.\n\nAs persona
 l pressures mount and Lana proves more exacting than forthcoming\, the bou
 ndaries between subject and writer\, truth and performance\, begin to blur
 . Allie is forced to reckon with how long she can remain in the background
  of other people’s stories\, and what it will cost her to finally step i
 nto her own.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only
 . Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179449
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
