BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-180909@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260412T123152Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Atlantic's Nick Thompson 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\
 nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180909\n\n5:00PM Recep
 tion\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into a wide-ranging conversation with Nic
 holas Thompson\, CEO of The Atlantic. During his tenure\, the publication
  has won the National Magazine Award for General Excellence three times\, 
 become one of the fastest-growing news organizations in the country\, and 
 reached record profitability and subscriber growth in its 157-year history
 . He is also the author of the national bestseller The Running Ground an
 d host of the podcast The Most Interesting Thing in AI\, where he explore
 s the rapidly evolving world of artificial intelligence.\n\nThompson will 
 be joined in conversation by Claire Hughes Johnson\, a technology leader a
 nd former Chief Operating Officer of Stripe. Together\, they will explore
  the forces shaping today’s media and technology landscapes - from the f
 uture of AI and innovation to the evolving role of storytelling and leader
 ship in a rapidly changing world.\n\n*This event is complimentary and rese
 rved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180909
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-180910@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260412T123152Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T150000
SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation: Networks\, Intelligence & the Future of D
 ecision-Making 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 100 spots le
 ft\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /180910\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat can we learn from the 
 individuals shaping AI\, enterprise transformation\, and modern engineerin
 g at the highest levels?\n\nIn the latest edition of 90 Minutes of Innovat
 ion\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI colu
 mnist - will lead a series of one-on-one conversations with three remarkab
 le leaders\, each offering a distinct perspective on innovation\, leadersh
 ip\, and the moment we’re in.\n\nJon Hirschtick\, founder of SolidWorks 
 and Onshape\, is a pioneering force in computer-aided design who has trans
 formed how engineers and designers build the world. An MIT alumnus\, he us
 ed winnings from the Institute’s legendary blackjack team to launch his 
 first company - an experience that later inspired the film 21.\n\nSandy Pe
 ntland\, MIT professor with appointments at MIT and Stanford\, and one of 
 the most cited data scientists globally\, whose work on human behavior\, s
 ocial networks\, and “reality mining” has fundamentally reshaped how w
 e understand trust\, cities\, and collective intelligence. He will speak o
 n his recent book\, Shared Wisdom: Cultural Evolution in the Age of AI.\n
 \nDavid Kenny\, Executive Chairman of Nielsen and former CEO of IBM Watson
 \, with prior leadership roles at Akamai and The Weather Channel\, has ope
 rated at the forefront of AI\, data\, and global enterprise transformation
 .\n\nThrough individual interviews\, the afternoon will explore their pers
 onal journeys\, the ideas that have defined their work\, and how each sees
  the rapidly evolving landscape of AI\, technology\, and innovation today.
  Expect an engaging\, insight-rich experience that connects lived experien
 ce with forward-looking perspective - offering a rare window into how thes
 e leaders think\, build\, and lead.\n\n*This event is complimentary and re
 served for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180910
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
