BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-182100@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260412T123152Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Finding Justice with New England Innocence Project
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 69 spots lef
 t\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/
 182100\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nAn evening that will chall
 enge what you think you know about justice - and redefine what it means to
  rebuild a life.\n\nHear firsthand from Sean Ellis and Edward Wright—two
  men who were wrongfully convicted\, spent decades incarcerated\, and ulti
 mately fought to reclaim their freedom. Their stories are deeply personal\
 , but also powerful reflections on systemic failure\, resilience\, and the
  long road to exoneration.\n\nSean Ellis\, whose case gained international
  attention through the Netflix docuseries Trial 4\, now leads advocacy ef
 forts through the Exoneree Network\, supporting others navigating life aft
 er incarceration. Edward Wright\, exonerated after 41 years\, taught himse
 lf the law while imprisoned - successfully fighting for his own freedom wh
 ile helping others do the same.\n\nThe conversation will be guided by Radh
 a Natarajan\, Executive Director of the New England Innocence Project\, wh
 ose work continues to confront bias and drive meaningful reform within the
  justice system.\n\nA rare opportunity to engage with voices at the forefr
 ont of justice reform - and to witness the strength\, clarity\, and humani
 ty behind these extraordinary journeys.\n\n*This event is complimentary an
 d reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182100
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
